# ================================================================
# Customer Retention & Churn Analysis
# Business Analytics Case Study — SQL + Power BI
#
# This project uses PostgreSQL and Power BI.
# This file documents the VS Code extensions and tools needed
# to run the project from VS Code.
#
# Install PostgreSQL driver for VS Code SQLTools:
#   1. Open VS Code
#   2. Extensions (Ctrl+Shift+X)
#   3. Search and install each extension below
# ================================================================

# ── VS Code Extensions (install via Extensions panel) ──────────
# SQLTools                    → mtxr.sqltools
# SQLTools PostgreSQL Driver  → mtxr.sqltools-driver-pg
# GitLens                     → eamodio.gitlens
# Markdown Preview Enhanced   → shd101wyy.markdown-preview-enhanced
# Rainbow CSV                 → mechatroner.rainbow-csv
# indent-rainbow              → oderwat.indent-rainbow

# ── External Tools (install separately) ────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL 16+   → https://www.postgresql.org/download/
# pgAdmin 4        → bundled with PostgreSQL installer
# Power BI Desktop → https://powerbi.microsoft.com/desktop/
# Git              → https://git-scm.com/download/win

# ── VS Code SQLTools connection settings ───────────────────────
# After installing SQLTools + PostgreSQL Driver, connect with:
#
#   Name    : churn_db (local)
#   Driver  : PostgreSQL
#   Server  : localhost
#   Port    : 5432
#   Database: churn_db
#   Username: postgres
#   Password: [datascience]
#
# Then run any .sql file with:
#   Ctrl+Shift+P → SQLTools: Run Current File

# ── Power BI PostgreSQL connector ──────────────────────────────
# Power BI requires the Npgsql driver to connect to PostgreSQL:
# Download: https://github.com/npgsql/npgsql/releases
# Install the .msi file, then restart Power BI Desktop.
# Connection: localhost | churn_db | Import mode

# ── Dataset ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IBM Telco Customer Churn (Kaggle - blastchar)
# https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/blastchar/telco-customer-churn
# Download the CSV, rename to telco_churn.csv
# Place at: data/raw/telco_churn.csv  (gitignored)
